{"id":"state-licensees-case-homes","title":"Who holds the State licence of each home in the nursing-home case","question":"Which companies hold the State licences of the 42 Bay Area homes whose assets are mostly owed by related companies, and do the licence names point to common sponsors?","finding":"The 42 case homes are held by 41 different licensees. 10 licensee names follow one pattern (place name + \"IDENCE OPCO, LLC\", e.g. San Franciscoidence Opco, LLC; Golden Gateidence Opco, LLC), 4 begin \"GHC of\", and Garfield Neurobehavioral Center and Morton Bakar Center are both licensed to Garfield Nursing Home Inc. San Francisco: San Francisco Post Acute (San Franciscoidence Opco, LLC); Victorian Post Acute (Golden Gateidence Opco, LLC); Central Gardens Post Acute (Golden California Healthcare, LLC).","how":"The 42 homes are the State facility numbers in the disclosure-report file names supplied for the case; each is found in the State health department's licence listing by its HCAI number. Licensee = BUSINESS_NAME; beds from HCAI Facility Profile Attributes where present, otherwise the listing's capacity. Licence effective date is the start of the current licence term.","limits":"A shared naming pattern is a name match only; it suggests, but does not prove, a common sponsor. Each home usually has its own operating company under the licensing rules; that is ordinary for chains and says nothing about how money moves. The listing shows current licensees only, not past ones.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"home","t":"Nursing home","type":"org"},{"k":"city","t":"City","type":"text"},{"k":"licensee","t":"State licensee","type":"org"},{"k":"entity","t":"Kind of entity","type":"text"},{"k":"beds","t":"Licensed beds","type":"int"},{"k":"firstLicensed","t":"First licensed","type":"date"},{"k":"licenceEffective","t":"Current licence from","type":"date"},{"k":"pattern","t":"Licensee name pattern","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"home":"Garfield Neurobehavioral Center","city":"Oakl